            "review_title": "Review at Cơm Nhà Sin",
            "review_text": "Adrian T\n49 contributions\n0\nBest dinner in Ho Chi Minh in a while\nOct 2025 • Solo\nIt’s been awhile since I last found a restaurant worth reviewing.\nFound this newly opened restaurant by chance in D1, HCMC.\nThe food is authentic home style Vietnamese food and it’s simply delicious.\nA very simple restaurant with hand painted murals but without the fancy and irrelevant decoration.\nThe duck soup cooked in coconut juice is a MUST TRY and so is the deep fried taro and shrimp served with lettuce & dipping sauce.\nAs a frequent visitor to Vietnam (over 70 times), I highly recommend this restaurant to those who wants to understand Vietnamese food other than the usual touristy food.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nLook for the owner, Chef Sin if you can’t decide what to order\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten October 19, 2025",
